{
 "manufacturer": "Greenheck",
 "manufacturer_slug": "greenheck",
 "model": "Dedicated Outdoor Air Systems (DOAS) - BACnet",
 "model_slug": "doas-bacnet-integration",
 "aliases": [
  "Greenheck DOAS",
  "DOAS",
  "DOAS_10.006",
  "485940"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Dedicated outdoor air system (DOAS)",
 "applies_to": "Greenheck dedicated outdoor air units whose factory controller runs the DOAS_10 program with BACnet licensed.",
 "summary": "Greenheck's DOAS units use a factory controller that can be licensed for BACnet. The BMS mainly enables the unit, commands occupancy, resets alarms and adjusts temperature, dehumidification and airflow setpoints; it can also take over fan speeds, the outdoor air damper and sensor values. A BMS watchdog must be written regularly whenever the BMS does that, or the unit alarms and returns to local control. The points list is the same on every unit regardless of heating and cooling options.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": "DOAS_10.006",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "BACnet must be licensed/enabled on the controller; without it the unit won't respond.",
  "Write BV-1 BMS_Watchdog = Active regularly; after the timeout (default 15 min) the unit alarms and falls back to local values.",
  "To use a BMS sensor value, set the matching *_Source_BMS binary to BMS, then write the *_from_BMS analog.",
  "Status bits (cooling/heating on, compressors, furnace stages, filter alarm, wheel, preheat, etc.) are packed into IV-6 to IV-11, with 16-bit AV copies.",
  "Unit_Status_Mode (AV-40) and LatestAlm (IV-5/AV-93) return codes; the source has the code tables.",
  "The guide only describes BBMD setup for IP networks; it does not say whether BACnet MS/TP is offered. Same controller family and object layout as the Greenheck IVE guide."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "BACnet Integration Guide for Dedicated Outdoor Air Systems",
  "doc_number": "Document 485940 (DOAS_10.006 Rev 5)",
  "revision_date": "2025-09",
  "url": "https://content.greenheck.com/public/DAMProd/Original/10017/485940_BACnetGuide.pdf"
 },
