 "integration": {
  "summary": "With BACnet licensed and set up on the controller, the minimum integration is to enable the unit (BV-2) and command occupancy (BV-3). Add alarm reset and global alarm monitoring, plus the temperature setpoint if needed. If the BMS will also drive fan speeds or the outdoor air damper, or send sensor values, it must keep writing the BMS watchdog, or the unit alarms and returns to local control.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 2",
    "name": "System_Enable",
    "why": "Enables or disables the unit"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 3",
    "name": "BMS_Occupancy_Command",
    "why": "Occupancy; Active = Unoccupied, Inactive = Occupied"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 1",
    "name": "Temperature_Setpoint",
    "why": "Occupied temperature setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 1",
    "name": "BMS_Watchdog",
    "why": "Heartbeat when BMS controls fans or sensors"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 4",
    "name": "Reset_All_Alarms",
    "why": "Remote alarm reset"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 40",
    "name": "Unit_Status_Mode",
    "why": "Current operating mode code"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 2",
    "name": "Supply_Temp_Analog_Input",
    "why": "Supply (discharge) air temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 23",
    "name": "Global_Alarm",
    "why": "Any active alarm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "IV 5",
    "name": "LatestAlm",
    "why": "Most recent alarm code"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "BV-2 System_Enable enables or disables the unit from the BMS; in disabled mode some protective sequences may still run. By default occupancy is expected from BV-3 BMS_Occupancy_Command. The controller can instead be set to an internal schedule, always occupied/unoccupied, or a digital input. With warm-up/cool-down enabled, the unit recirculates after the occupied command until it reaches setpoint or the timer (default 30 min) ends.",
  "heartbeat": "BV-1 BMS_Watchdog must be written to True (1) regularly whenever the BMS commands fan speeds or damper positions or sends sensor values. If it stays False longer than the Timeout Delay (15 minutes, adjustable), an alarm is raised and the controller falls back to local control and local sensor values. BV-24 shows watchdog status. If the relinquish-default-on-comm-loss option is enabled, priority arrays are cleared 5 minutes after the watchdog goes inactive.",
  "remote_sensors": "For each sensor, set its source-select binary to BMS (BV-7 to BV-16, e.g. BV-8 Outside_Temp_Source_BMS, BV-16 Space_Temp_Source_BMS). Then write the matching *_from_BMS analog (AV-26 to AV-35, e.g. AV-27 outside temp, AV-35 space temp, AV-33 space RH, AV-30/31 space CO2). The watchdog must be satisfied; if it isn't, the controller reverts to the local sensor (if installed and valid) or to local control. Fan speeds and the outdoor air damper are taken over the same way with BV-17/18/19 plus AV-36/37/38.",
  "setup": [
   "The controller must have BACnet licensed and configured; otherwise get the license/config files from the rep (alarm 82 = BACnet license not installed).",
   "BBMD and foreign-device registration, relinquish defaults and COV increments are in the Advanced BACnet Settings menu (Main Menu > Control Variables > Advanced > Network Settings > Advanced Settings).",
   "COV increments are shared by all objects with the same engineering unit.",
   "For BMS supply-air reset, set the reset mode (IV-1) to No Reset and write the temperature setpoint (AV-1)."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "The points list is the same on every unit, so points for options a unit lacks are meaningless on it.",
   "Writing too often triggers alarm 32 (BMS Frequent Writes); reduce write traffic.",
   "Status bits are packed into IV-6 to IV-11; use the 16-bit AV copies (AV-94 to AV-105) if the BMS can't read 32-bit integers.",
   "Unit_Status_Mode (AV-40) can rotate between active modes every 3 seconds.",
   "Without Return to Default enabled, the controller boots after a power loss with the last written values."
  ]
 },
 "page": "https://easybacnet.com/bacnet-points-lists/greenheck/doas-bacnet-integration",
